      "summary": "The root Linux worker launch can fail before parsing when network namespace creation succeeds, causing intake to reject all PDFs on that deployment.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 128,
          "message": "The root Linux launch path combines `unshare -r` with a later switch to UID 65534, which is not mapped in that user namespace. Valid PDFs therefore fail whenever network namespace creation is available.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "On Linux, CreateStartInfo adds `unshare -rn` before `setpriv --reuid=65534` when network namespaces are available and the API runs as root. `unshare -r` maps the caller to root in a new user namespace; that mapping does not include UID 65534.",
            "failureScenario": "When the API runs as root on Linux with working network namespaces and setpriv, the worker's setpriv command cannot switch to unmapped UID 65534 and exits before parsing. Intake then returns a retryable failure for every PDF, including valid ones."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
